1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,067
<i> Go ahead, shoot.</i>

2
00:00:01,233 --> 00:00:02,133
<i> Don't aim at him.</i>

3
00:00:02,267 --> 00:00:03,533
<i>That's Andrew Dizon,
a famous vlogger.</i>

4
00:00:03,667 --> 00:00:04,633
<i>All right, Sir,
please come in.</i>

5
00:00:04,767 --> 00:00:05,567
<i> Andrew?</i>

6
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:06,633
<i>Yvette, what are you doing here?</i>

7
00:00:06,767 --> 00:00:08,300
<i> I'm here for Hope Circle.</i>

8
00:00:08,433 --> 00:00:09,867
<i>What about you,
what are you doing here?</i>

9
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,767
<i>Long story, Yvette.
Anyway, I have to go.</i>

10
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:13,333
<i> I've got a bonus.</i>

11
00:00:13,467 --> 00:00:17,400
<i>I already know where that
leech Golda is hiding.</i>

12
00:00:17,533 --> 00:00:20,867
<i>She's here right under my nose.</i>

13
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:21,933
<i> Braggy is here.</i>

14
00:00:22,067 --> 00:00:23,400
<i> Where are you, Golda?</i>

15
00:00:23,533 --> 00:00:26,067
<i>Wait, didn't I tell all of you
to step outside?</i>

16
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:28,600
<i>Joey, one of the syndicates
looking for you is here.</i>

17
00:00:28,733 --> 00:00:30,767
<i>I'll take all the heavy calibers
in your arsenal</i>

18
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:33,100
<i>as long as the transaction
stays clean.</i>

19
00:00:33,233 --> 00:00:34,267
<i> Because if anything leaks,</i>

20
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:35,567
<i> the deal stops</i>

21
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:37,067
<i> and so does the breathing</i>

22
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:38,367
<i> of whoever starts talking.</i>

23
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,000
<i> Don't push me.</i>

24
00:00:40,133 --> 00:00:42,767
<i>I might smash that jar
over your head.</i>

25
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:44,467
<i>- It's on.
- I'll handle it.</i>

26
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:46,533
<i>- It's a deal.
- Congrats, boys!</i>

27
00:00:46,667 --> 00:00:48,133
<i>- Braggy...
- Who's this?</i>

28
00:00:48,267 --> 00:00:50,367
<i>Let's just say I know what
you've been cooking up</i>

29
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:51,500
<i> with Godfather.</i>

30
00:00:51,633 --> 00:00:53,200
<i>How did someone find out about
our transaction?</i>

31
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:55,133
<i>You liars!
You're an animal, Godfather!</i>

32
00:00:55,267 --> 00:00:56,167
<i>You're going straight to hell
now!</i>

33
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:57,467
<i> You should go first!</i>

34
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:59,000
<i>My mother, I need to go to her.</i>

35
00:00:59,133 --> 00:01:00,167
<i> I'll be the one going in.</i>

36
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:02,433
<i>Andrew wouldn't abandon Mom,
right?</i>

37
00:01:02,567 --> 00:01:05,300
<i>After I fill
Braganza with bullets,</i>

38
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:07,200
<i> you're next.</i>

39
00:01:07,367 --> 00:01:09,367
<i>You have nowhere left to run,
Braganza!</i>

40
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:10,333
<i> Theresa?</i>

41
00:01:10,467 --> 00:01:11,800
<i>I can't let Theresa
get away again.</i>

42
00:01:12,133 --> 00:01:12,733
<i> I'm going to catch her.</i>

43
00:01:12,867 --> 00:01:13,833
<i> We can't get trapped here!</i>

44
00:01:13,967 --> 00:01:16,067
<i> Chase that animal!</i>

45
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,067
<i> Miss Clarissa, let's go.</i>

46
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:18,467
<i> Don't let her get out alive!</i>

47
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:20,600
<i> Find Golda!</i>

48
00:01:22,333 --> 00:01:32,300
<i> [OBB]</i>

49
00:01:39,467 --> 00:01:43,333
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

50
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:44,767
Be honest.

51
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:47,133
Were you really going to
leave me at that party?

52
00:01:47,533 --> 00:01:49,033
What do you think?

53
00:01:49,167 --> 00:01:50,033
They were already shooting
at each other.

54
00:01:50,167 --> 00:01:52,300
Do you think I'd still
look for you?

55
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,467
I guess there won't be
a next date.

56
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:01,200
[TIRES SCREECH]

57
00:02:01,333 --> 00:02:03,867
What the hell? You idiot!
Are you trying to kill yourself?

58
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,500
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

59
00:02:11,667 --> 00:02:13,567
Are you guys sure you're okay?

60
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:17,967
Miss Clarissa...

61
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:20,167
why were you at the party today?

62
00:02:20,933 --> 00:02:22,167
She's my assistant.

63
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:23,567
She's with me.

64
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:26,067
Tomas wasn't around,
so I brought her with me.

65
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:29,233
Oh, why do you know Clarissa?

66
00:02:29,367 --> 00:02:32,167
[♪UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING♪]

67
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:35,000
I did an expose on her husband,

68
00:02:35,133 --> 00:02:37,233
Major Miguel Delgado.

69
00:02:42,733 --> 00:02:46,033
Thank you, Boss Idol Andrew.

70
00:02:46,633 --> 00:02:49,067
If you hadn't arrived,

71
00:02:49,233 --> 00:02:53,100
I don't know what might have
happened to me.

72
00:02:53,233 --> 00:02:55,900
Why did this even happen?

73
00:02:56,033 --> 00:02:57,433
Everything was going fine
at the party earlier,

74
00:02:57,567 --> 00:02:59,800
then suddenly people
started shooting.

75
00:03:00,467 --> 00:03:02,033
There could be many reasons,
Yvette.

76
00:03:02,167 --> 00:03:03,900
What do you mean?

77
00:03:04,033 --> 00:03:06,800
And what were you doing
at the party earlier?

78
00:03:06,933 --> 00:03:09,000
Were you even invited?

79
00:03:09,433 --> 00:03:10,733
I was there for an expose.

80
00:03:10,867 --> 00:03:12,467
But something went wrong,
betrayal,

81
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:14,367
a turf war,

82
00:03:15,367 --> 00:03:17,233
a deal gone bad.

83
00:03:17,633 --> 00:03:19,900
[REVVING]

84
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:24,300
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

85
00:03:30,767 --> 00:03:34,733
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

86
00:03:46,233 --> 00:03:47,267
- Who are you?
- Wait...

87
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:48,733
Where's Theresa?

88
00:03:48,867 --> 00:03:50,400
Wait, Theresa?

89
00:03:50,533 --> 00:03:52,100
I don't know any Theresa.

90
00:03:52,233 --> 00:03:55,267
Wait, don't you know
Vicente Alcala?

91
00:03:55,833 --> 00:03:57,967
He's an arms dealer,

92
00:03:58,100 --> 00:03:59,400
also known as Godfather.

93
00:03:59,533 --> 00:04:00,900
- What?
- Ah...

94
00:04:01,433 --> 00:04:03,367
He sells guns?

95
00:04:04,833 --> 00:04:06,567
Illegally.

96
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:08,233
It can't be!
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

97
00:04:08,367 --> 00:04:11,467
As far as I know, he's a very
successful businessman.

98
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:14,167
That's why I'm trying to get him
as a sponsor

99
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:16,400
for my foundation.

100
00:04:16,533 --> 00:04:21,633
Oh my, Ma'am.
That man sounds dangerous.

101
00:04:22,467 --> 00:04:25,567
That's why, Yvette,
you should always be careful

102
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:29,600
and examine the people
you deal with.

103
00:04:30,667 --> 00:04:34,100
Sometimes, wolves hide
under sheep's clothing.

104
00:04:34,233 --> 00:04:38,600
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

105
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:46,100
The one who was with you,
where is she?

106
00:04:46,233 --> 00:04:48,400
She left already.
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

107
00:04:50,467 --> 00:04:52,433
Her name is Lisa, not Theresa.

108
00:04:52,567 --> 00:04:53,667
Where did she go?

109
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:56,267
I don't know, promise.

110
00:04:57,067 --> 00:05:01,167
[REVVING]
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

111
00:05:03,233 --> 00:05:05,067
<i> I was worried about you</i>

112
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:07,067
<i> so I looked for you,</i>

113
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:10,467
<i>and then you just left me there?</i>

114
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:11,967
<i> That's mean!</i>

115
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:16,033
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

116
00:05:21,967 --> 00:05:23,367
[PHONE RINGS]

117
00:05:23,500 --> 00:05:24,900
<i> Why?</i>

118
00:05:25,033 --> 00:05:27,033
<i> I need a ride, right now.</i>

119
00:05:27,167 --> 00:05:28,767
<i> You're leaving me?</i>

120
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:31,367
<i> Send someone here right now.</i>

121
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:33,300
<i> I need to get out of here.</i>

122
00:05:34,633 --> 00:05:37,933
[REVVING]

123
00:05:39,733 --> 00:05:42,133
Let's go straight
to the warehouse.

124
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:44,633
Are you sure
you want to get off here?

125
00:05:45,733 --> 00:05:47,667
Yes, Yevtte, I'm okay here.

126
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:50,800
Thank you again,
Boss Idol Andrew.

127
00:05:53,033 --> 00:05:56,767
At least I can somehow make up
for what I did to your family.

128
00:05:59,367 --> 00:06:04,100
Miss Clarissa, I'm sorry
if I hurt you.

129
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:09,200
You only did that because you
were angry at the police.

130
00:06:09,833 --> 00:06:13,500
That's what my daughter
Joey told me.

131
00:06:14,867 --> 00:06:17,633
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

132
00:06:17,767 --> 00:06:18,800
Actually, what I want to do

133
00:06:18,933 --> 00:06:21,000
is prove that

134
00:06:21,133 --> 00:06:23,633
I was wrong about Major Miguel.

135
00:06:23,767 --> 00:06:25,700
And when that happens,

136
00:06:25,833 --> 00:06:29,833
I'll be the first one
to report the whole truth.

137
00:06:31,167 --> 00:06:32,600
I'm sure you will.

138
00:06:32,733 --> 00:06:36,400
I know you, and you always tell
the truth.

139
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:39,767
But for now, Clarissa
and I will head home.

140
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:42,733
We'll go ahead,
and you should too.

141
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:44,400
It's okay.

142
00:06:44,533 --> 00:06:46,167
Take care.

143
00:06:47,233 --> 00:06:51,633
[PHONE BUZZING]

144
00:06:51,767 --> 00:06:53,800
- Hello, Andrew?
- Hello, Joey?

145
00:06:54,633 --> 00:06:56,067
Where are you?

146
00:06:56,567 --> 00:06:57,833
Are you safe?

147
00:06:57,967 --> 00:06:59,300
Yes.
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

148
00:06:59,433 --> 00:07:01,400
But why are you
only contacting me now?

149
00:07:01,533 --> 00:07:02,833
I've been calling you
for a while.

150
00:07:02,967 --> 00:07:03,900
<i> How's Mom?</i>

151
00:07:04,033 --> 00:07:05,500
Well, they're safe.

152
00:07:05,633 --> 00:07:07,900
She's on her way home
with my sister.

153
00:07:08,367 --> 00:07:09,800
That's good.

154
00:07:11,333 --> 00:07:12,433
All right, go back here now.

155
00:07:12,567 --> 00:07:14,033
We need you.

156
00:07:14,467 --> 00:07:15,867
Why? Is there a problem?

157
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,900
Just hurry up.

158
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:26,500
Where's Joey?

159
00:07:26,633 --> 00:07:28,100
- I have the same question.
- Oh...

160
00:07:28,233 --> 00:07:29,200
Oh, looks like these two
are already here.

161
00:07:29,333 --> 00:07:30,267
So?

162
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:32,300
Did you catch Theresa?

163
00:07:32,433 --> 00:07:36,467
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

164
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:37,967
I lost her.

165
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:41,767
TOTGA, the one that got away.

166
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:46,133
We didn't gain anything
from this mission.

167
00:07:46,267 --> 00:07:47,467
Wrong...

168
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:49,700
We still got something.

169
00:07:51,433 --> 00:07:56,033
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

170
00:08:03,433 --> 00:08:05,367
Let me go!

171
00:08:05,500 --> 00:08:07,267
What the hell?

172
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:11,667
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

173
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,900
Sir...

174
00:08:16,567 --> 00:08:18,267
Sir, we will just use
the restroom.

175
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:21,067
Stand there, stay there.

176
00:08:23,933 --> 00:08:25,300
Miguel.

177
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:28,333
Trigger wants to
talk to you tomorrow.

178
00:08:28,933 --> 00:08:31,467
And then, you will
gang up on me again?

179
00:08:31,867 --> 00:08:33,333
Think whatever you want.

180
00:08:33,467 --> 00:08:35,633
That's just what
he told me to say.

181
00:08:36,033 --> 00:08:38,833
It's up to you
whether you go or not.

182
00:08:38,967 --> 00:08:40,833
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:08:40,967 --> 00:08:42,500
Hey Miguel, aren't you done yet?

184
00:08:42,633 --> 00:08:43,633
Hurry up!

185
00:08:43,767 --> 00:08:45,500
You guys, aren't you done
using the restroom yet?

186
00:08:45,633 --> 00:08:46,400
All done.

187
00:08:46,533 --> 00:08:48,400
- Okay, okay, Sir.
- Okay.

188
00:08:48,533 --> 00:08:49,767
Sir.

189
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:53,867
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

190
00:08:57,233 --> 00:08:59,067
Let me get out of here!

191
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:00,733
What the hell?

192
00:09:00,867 --> 00:09:02,400
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

193
00:09:02,533 --> 00:09:04,200
Why is she here?

194
00:09:06,067 --> 00:09:07,533
How did you capture Golda?

195
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:13,067
- [SHRIEKS]
- [TIRES SCREECH]

196
00:09:14,567 --> 00:09:15,467
[GROANS]

197
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:17,200
<i>- Miss...
- Are you okay?</i>

198
00:09:19,067 --> 00:09:20,467
<i> Golda?</i>

199
00:09:21,367 --> 00:09:23,467
That's why
we brought Golda here.

200
00:09:23,600 --> 00:09:25,433
You tricked me!

201
00:09:25,567 --> 00:09:26,800
Not really.

202
00:09:26,933 --> 00:09:28,400
So stop acting up.

203
00:09:28,567 --> 00:09:29,700
Exactly.

204
00:09:29,833 --> 00:09:32,067
You asked us to help you get
away from there, didn't you?

205
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,900
Well, that's exactly
what we did.

206
00:09:34,033 --> 00:09:35,900
You haven't even said
thank you yet.

207
00:09:36,033 --> 00:09:37,133
But there's something else
I want to hear,

208
00:09:37,267 --> 00:09:38,967
not just thank you.

209
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:40,300
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

210
00:09:40,433 --> 00:09:42,333
We already helped you.

211
00:09:42,467 --> 00:09:43,567
So can you...

212
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:44,733
tell me everything you know

213
00:09:44,867 --> 00:09:46,867
about how my father was set up.

214
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,600
Start from the beginning.

215
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:52,367
And don't leave any detail.

216
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:54,900
Yes, yes, what they said.

217
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:59,033
Start talking.

218
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:04,200
All the transactions
happen at the spa.

219
00:10:05,967 --> 00:10:07,433
And Loloy,

220
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:09,533
he was my contact

221
00:10:10,100 --> 00:10:11,733
who delivered the supplies.

222
00:10:11,867 --> 00:10:14,667
Supplies meaning drugs?
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

223
00:10:19,467 --> 00:10:21,733
And that's where
your father caught me.

224
00:10:23,067 --> 00:10:25,000
But instead of throwing me
in jail,

225
00:10:25,633 --> 00:10:28,233
he made me his informant
in exchange for my freedom.

226
00:10:29,767 --> 00:10:30,633
But...

227
00:10:31,667 --> 00:10:33,267
but Parak found out.

228
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:34,500
Godfather Diego.

229
00:10:34,667 --> 00:10:36,567
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

230
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:39,933
<i>I was just cornered,
that's why I gave the tip.</i>

231
00:10:40,067 --> 00:10:42,467
<i>I'm sorry, Diego,
I'll keep quiet...</i>

232
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,333
<i> just please don't kill me.</i>

233
00:10:44,467 --> 00:10:46,133
<i>I don't want you to stay quiet.</i>

234
00:10:46,267 --> 00:10:48,000
<i>What I want is for you to sing.</i>

235
00:10:48,133 --> 00:10:50,467
<i> And I'll dictate the lyrics.</i>

236
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:52,600
He threatened me!

237
00:10:52,733 --> 00:10:54,200
He threatened me,
that's why...

238
00:10:54,333 --> 00:10:57,767
I started making up stories
to ruin Miguel.

239
00:10:58,900 --> 00:10:59,933
Then...

240
00:11:00,067 --> 00:11:02,033
when Miguel was imprisoned,

241
00:11:02,167 --> 00:11:04,033
that's when I went into hiding

242
00:11:04,167 --> 00:11:05,267
because I knew...

243
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:07,933
I knew I'd be next for Berdugo.

244
00:11:08,467 --> 00:11:09,767
Berdugo?

245
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:11,967
He's the leader
of the syndicates.

246
00:11:12,667 --> 00:11:15,733
How about Theresa Park or Lisa?

247
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:20,500
I don't know anyone
named Lisa or Theresa.

248
00:11:21,700 --> 00:11:24,633
The only one I know is Loloy.

249
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:26,233
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

250
00:11:26,367 --> 00:11:28,633
Most likely, Berdugo was the one
who set your father up.

251
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:30,967
Then who is Berdugo?

252
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:32,667
What's his real name?

253
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:35,533
Nothing, I don't know.

254
00:11:35,667 --> 00:11:37,000
I've never even talked to him.

255
00:11:37,133 --> 00:11:38,700
I've never seen him in person,

256
00:11:38,833 --> 00:11:40,800
not even on the phone,
I never talked to him.

257
00:11:40,933 --> 00:11:42,567
Can you stop lying!

258
00:11:42,733 --> 00:11:44,233
Admit everything!

259
00:11:44,367 --> 00:11:45,967
I'm not lying to you!

260
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:49,133
What do you want? I already told
you everything I know!

261
00:11:49,267 --> 00:11:50,333
If you don't want to believe me,

262
00:11:50,467 --> 00:11:52,600
then that's your problem!

263
00:11:52,733 --> 00:11:54,933
You know what,
we're all exhausted.

264
00:11:55,067 --> 00:11:56,833
So much happened tonight.

265
00:11:56,967 --> 00:11:59,600
Maybe it's better
if we just rest.

266
00:11:59,833 --> 00:12:02,367
Joey, I'll talk to you tomorrow.

267
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:04,733
I'll watch Golda,
I'll handle it.

268
00:12:04,867 --> 00:12:06,533
Let's get some rest.

269
00:12:06,667 --> 00:12:10,667
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

270
00:12:13,233 --> 00:12:15,267
Golda, are you there?

271
00:12:16,467 --> 00:12:19,267
Where else would I go, huh?

272
00:12:19,667 --> 00:12:20,800
Just making sure.

273
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:34,200
Is she not done yet?
I still need to talk to her.

274
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:36,133
Joey...

275
00:12:37,733 --> 00:12:40,333
I think it would be better if
I'm the one who talks to Golda

276
00:12:40,467 --> 00:12:42,733
so she can become our witness.

277
00:12:42,867 --> 00:12:44,167
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

278
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:46,733
Why again?
Because I'm emotional right now.

279
00:12:47,367 --> 00:12:50,867
Well, obviously my anger
comes from somewhere.

280
00:12:51,133 --> 00:12:52,133
Yes, there is.

281
00:12:52,367 --> 00:12:54,067
And we all know that.

282
00:12:54,633 --> 00:12:58,033
She ruined your father
and your whole family.

283
00:12:58,600 --> 00:13:01,933
But we have to strategize
to get Golda on our side.

284
00:13:02,067 --> 00:13:03,400
Yeah, he's right.

285
00:13:03,533 --> 00:13:06,733
Scaring and antagonizing her
won't be helpful.

286
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,033
Okay, fine.

287
00:13:10,167 --> 00:13:12,433
For Dad's sake,
I won't go after her.

288
00:13:12,567 --> 00:13:15,500
Just make sure she cooperates.

289
00:13:15,633 --> 00:13:19,867
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

290
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:29,500
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

291
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:34,167
-[KNOCK]
-Golda, what are you doing?

292
00:13:35,333 --> 00:13:37,367
- [KNOCKS]
- Golda.

293
00:13:39,633 --> 00:13:41,033
- [KNOCKS]
- Hey.

294
00:13:41,267 --> 00:13:43,500
I'm just going to take a shower,
okay?

295
00:13:45,867 --> 00:13:47,033
Okay.

296
00:13:47,567 --> 00:13:57,500
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

297
00:14:03,833 --> 00:14:09,267
[PHONE RINGING]

298
00:14:09,400 --> 00:14:11,667
Oh, Joey, how are you?

299
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:13,900
<i>Hello, Mom?
How are you?</i>

300
00:14:14,033 --> 00:14:15,067
I'm okay.

301
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:17,033
Oh! Joey...

302
00:14:17,167 --> 00:14:20,200
<i>You won't believe what happened
to me last night.</i>

303
00:14:20,333 --> 00:14:22,367
I almost died!

304
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:25,000
What? How?

305
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:28,733
My boss brought me to a party,

306
00:14:28,900 --> 00:14:29,967
<i> then chaos broke out.</i>

307
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:32,567
There was an actual shootout.

308
00:14:32,700 --> 00:14:33,767
We didn't know

309
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:36,900
that the one who invited us was
part of a syndicate.

310
00:14:37,033 --> 00:14:38,300
<i> But...</i>

311
00:14:38,433 --> 00:14:40,400
someone saved me, Boss Budol...

312
00:14:40,533 --> 00:14:42,033
I mean...

313
00:14:42,167 --> 00:14:42,933
<i> Boss Idol.</i>

314
00:14:43,067 --> 00:14:45,200
Do you remember
my boss's brother?

315
00:14:47,633 --> 00:14:48,400
Ah...

316
00:14:48,933 --> 00:14:50,833
You weren't hurt, Mom?

317
00:14:50,967 --> 00:14:52,733
No, child, I'm safe.

318
00:14:52,867 --> 00:14:55,500
Andrew saved me.

319
00:14:55,633 --> 00:14:56,400
Ah...

320
00:14:56,533 --> 00:14:57,767
And you know what,

321
00:14:57,900 --> 00:14:59,900
he apologized to me

322
00:15:00,033 --> 00:15:02,967
for what he did
to your father, to us.

323
00:15:03,733 --> 00:15:07,133
I could see and feel
his sincerity.

324
00:15:08,433 --> 00:15:09,833
He's actually kind, isn't he?

325
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:11,667
<i> And brave.</i>

326
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:13,633
<i> You know,</i>

327
00:15:13,767 --> 00:15:15,433
<i> he never left my side</i>

328
00:15:15,567 --> 00:15:18,033
<i>even though his sister
was there.</i>

329
00:15:26,833 --> 00:15:28,600
- This is crazy.
- We're already hungry.

330
00:15:28,733 --> 00:15:30,033
What a shameless.

331
00:15:30,167 --> 00:15:40,133
[PEOPLE CHATTERING]

332
00:15:48,367 --> 00:15:50,600
What is this, cellmate?

333
00:15:50,733 --> 00:15:51,767
Is this all we get?

334
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:55,000
That's enough, that's enough.
Break it up, break it up.

335
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:58,400
That's enough, that's enough.

336
00:15:58,533 --> 00:16:00,233
Stop! Stop!

337
00:16:00,367 --> 00:16:02,700
- Stop! Stop!
- That's too much, Sir!

338
00:16:06,033 --> 00:16:07,633
What do you want?

339
00:16:09,467 --> 00:16:12,533
You're the one I'm asking
what you need.

340
00:16:15,267 --> 00:16:17,300
You saved my life, right?

341
00:16:18,333 --> 00:16:21,167
In return,
I'll give you one favor.

342
00:16:24,167 --> 00:16:25,533
Only one?

343
00:16:28,733 --> 00:16:30,800
Nothing unlimited here.

344
00:16:32,167 --> 00:16:32,933
So if I were you,

345
00:16:33,067 --> 00:16:35,300
think carefully
about what you want.

346
00:16:36,033 --> 00:16:38,000
I'll come back for your answer,
think about it.

347
00:16:45,467 --> 00:16:46,900
Let's eat!

348
00:16:48,967 --> 00:16:52,267
Sorry, this is all
I managed to prepare.

349
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:54,567
We didn't really have food here.

350
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:56,600
Just for lunch,
I'll make it up next time.

351
00:16:56,733 --> 00:16:58,167
Come on.

352
00:16:58,300 --> 00:16:59,767
It's fine.

353
00:17:00,733 --> 00:17:02,800
Thanks for preparing this.

354
00:17:05,667 --> 00:17:06,833
Hey, Peter!

355
00:17:06,967 --> 00:17:08,033
Let's eat.

356
00:17:08,667 --> 00:17:09,833
Go ahead.

357
00:17:09,967 --> 00:17:12,000
The one I'm watching still
hasn't come out.

358
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:13,467
I'll wait for Golda.

359
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:19,767
Joey...

360
00:17:20,233 --> 00:17:21,933
I'm just going outside
for a bit.

361
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:32,433
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

362
00:17:55,033 --> 00:17:58,800
Where are you going?

363
00:17:58,933 --> 00:18:02,667
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

364
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:04,233
What is this?

365
00:18:04,467 --> 00:18:06,367
Why are you doing this?

366
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:07,833
Do you know that
what you're doing to me

367
00:18:07,967 --> 00:18:09,067
is illegal detention?

368
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:11,233
I'll report you!

369
00:18:11,667 --> 00:18:13,333
To whom?

370
00:18:13,933 --> 00:18:15,467
To the police?

371
00:18:16,600 --> 00:18:18,233
Go! Do it.

372
00:18:19,133 --> 00:18:21,800
Just make sure no one is waiting
for you outside.

373
00:18:22,733 --> 00:18:24,433
And pray...

374
00:18:24,567 --> 00:18:29,100
that the cop you run to isn't
under Berdugo or Godfather.

375
00:18:30,833 --> 00:18:32,133
Yes, I know.

376
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:34,633
Godfather is angry at you

377
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:37,133
and he's having you hunted.

378
00:18:38,533 --> 00:18:40,433
Why is he mad at me, huh?

379
00:18:40,567 --> 00:18:42,167
I didn't do anything wrong.

380
00:18:42,300 --> 00:18:44,067
I didn't double-cross them.

381
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:45,867
I swear!

382
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:50,033
Even that Braganza guy
is probably blaming me.

383
00:18:50,367 --> 00:18:52,500
He didn't even let me explain.

384
00:18:52,633 --> 00:18:54,733
Why? Do you think...

385
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:56,200
if you meet them in person

386
00:18:56,333 --> 00:18:58,000
they'll listen to you?

387
00:18:58,400 --> 00:19:01,300
They might just delete you
permanently.

388
00:19:02,867 --> 00:19:06,133
You know what kind of people
they are, Golda.

389
00:19:07,067 --> 00:19:10,300
You know what they're capable
of doing.

390
00:19:15,033 --> 00:19:16,967
Golda, all of them
are looking for you.

391
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:21,567
All of them want you dead.

392
00:19:22,633 --> 00:19:25,400
Actually, Joey and I are
the only incentive

393
00:19:25,533 --> 00:19:27,267
to stay alive.

394
00:19:27,767 --> 00:19:29,267
So if I were you,

395
00:19:29,433 --> 00:19:33,433
I'd really think about
whose side I'm on.

396
00:19:42,700 --> 00:19:44,633
You eat first.

397
00:19:57,267 --> 00:19:58,667
I think she escaped.

398
00:19:58,800 --> 00:20:00,133
What? How?

399
00:20:00,267 --> 00:20:02,667
She must have gone
through the window!

400
00:20:02,833 --> 00:20:04,133
No, I thought she was just
taking a shower.

401
00:20:04,267 --> 00:20:05,567
The shower is still running.

402
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:07,400
Come on, let's find her!

403
00:20:07,533 --> 00:20:08,600
Let's go!

404
00:20:08,733 --> 00:20:10,167
Jin Ho!

405
00:20:18,767 --> 00:20:21,767
You really thought you could
slip past us, huh?

406
00:20:21,900 --> 00:20:24,167
You've got some nerve!

407
00:20:24,300 --> 00:20:25,733
Good thing you saw her.

408
00:20:25,967 --> 00:20:26,967
Of course.

409
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:29,900
And she's willing
to be our witness.

410
00:20:31,300 --> 00:20:33,033
All right, fine.

411
00:20:33,833 --> 00:20:35,900
Just don't tie me up.

412
00:20:36,067 --> 00:20:40,000
And make sure I'm safe
from the people hunting me.

413
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:42,067
I don't want to die yet.

414
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:44,333
If you're just saying that
to trick us,

415
00:20:44,600 --> 00:20:45,533
we'll be the ones to tell

416
00:20:45,667 --> 00:20:47,733
the people you're hiding from
where you are.

417
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:50,800
This is the only thing
I'm asking in return

418
00:20:50,933 --> 00:20:53,300
for everything you did
to my family.

419
00:20:53,767 --> 00:20:55,633
So you should cooperate.

420
00:20:55,767 --> 00:20:58,200
No more running, no more tricks.

421
00:21:16,233 --> 00:21:18,700
Godfather and Braganza
are now feuding.

422
00:21:18,833 --> 00:21:20,067
The two of them are going
to kill each other.

423
00:21:20,200 --> 00:21:22,000
But what you're asking is
difficult.

424
00:21:22,133 --> 00:21:23,400
It's hard to find Berdugo.

425
00:21:23,533 --> 00:21:25,000
No one stays hidden forever.

426
00:21:25,133 --> 00:21:26,900
According to our
reliable source,

427
00:21:27,033 --> 00:21:29,367
the wanted drug dealer
in Bolagos

428
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:30,933
is known by the name Loloy.

429
00:21:31,067 --> 00:21:33,533
We need to find out
who the whistleblower is.

430
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:35,000
Tell me, who is your source?

431
00:21:35,133 --> 00:21:37,400
Brother, you know
I don't burn my sources.

432
00:21:37,533 --> 00:21:39,533
Besides, you won't be
involved anyway...

433
00:21:39,667 --> 00:21:41,433
unless you're doing
something illegal.

434
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:42,600
Didn't he say anything?

435
00:21:42,733 --> 00:21:43,967
- He did.
- Golda.

436
00:21:44,100 --> 00:21:45,167
I'll be the one watching you.

437
00:21:45,300 --> 00:21:47,133
Are you really watching me,

438
00:21:47,267 --> 00:21:48,200
or your girlfriend?

439
00:21:48,333 --> 00:21:49,633
- Ah...
- Yes.

440
00:21:49,767 --> 00:21:50,867
They're not together!

441
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,200
Boss Budol is the one
who scam me!

442
00:21:53,333 --> 00:21:55,167
- Young love.
- My contact said

443
00:21:55,300 --> 00:21:57,467
<i>Golda has already given
a statement.</i>

444
00:21:57,600 --> 00:21:59,433
We have to make sure
that her testimony

445
00:21:59,567 --> 00:22:00,700
doesn't see the light of day.

446
00:22:00,833 --> 00:22:02,100
Matias, you know the drill.

447
00:22:02,233 --> 00:22:03,167
Copy, Berdugo.

448
00:22:03,300 --> 00:22:04,933
There's someone,
are they still there?

449
00:22:05,067 --> 00:22:05,967
They might break in.

450
00:22:06,100 --> 00:22:07,700
Just don't make any noise.
